t from year to year (CV 0.41).","It converts 39% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.58x.","ROE of 294% is amplified by 20.1x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 1.3% of revenue on R&D and 1.8% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.6x net debt to EBITDA ($2.2B of cash against $4.7B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 7.9x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 7.2% over 3 years, 2.0% over 5 years and 4.0% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 75% of profits supports about 15.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 7.7% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.00 and a backlog worth 15% of annual revenue.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 7.9% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 39, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $3.9M sold).","It returns 3.3% a year to shareholders (2.3% in buybacks and 1.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 4.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 8,000 employees, each generates about $384K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 6.2% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $149K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.5M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $7K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":67,"head":"Watch: composite 54, above the 39 line, but only 3% below fair value; it becomes a buy below $181.","pros":["Composite 54, above the 39 line (ga